# The content release and the module that reads it.
#
# content/release.json is a generated learner copy of a content release
# (ADR-0028). NEVER EDIT IT BY HAND. A change to it is a content change
# wearing a JSON costume: to change content, change the content repository
# and cut a release there, then regenerate this file from a clean checkout
# of that content@ tag and open a pull request with the result:
#
#   npm run build -- --target learner --release content@YYYY.MM.N --out ../web/content/release.json
#
# npm test recomputes the file's content hash, so a hand edit fails CI. Review
# it as a content release: which release and commit it names, and what
# learners will see. lib/content.ts is its only importer and changes what every
# learner is shown; lib/redirects.ts turns it into redirects, and a permanent
# one is remembered by browsers for good.
/content/                       @muhammaduzair11 @junaidaslam2006
/lib/content.ts                 @muhammaduzair11 @junaidaslam2006
/lib/redirects.ts               @muhammaduzair11 @junaidaslam2006

